      en: "The National Museum of Iran in Tehran was inaugurated in 1937 and houses the country's largest archaeological collection. The building was designed by French architect André Godard. The museum's exhibits span from the Paleolithic era to the Islamic period. Key artifacts include the Salt Man, a 2,500-year-old mummy, and the Cyrus Cylinder. The museum has two wings: the Museum of Ancient Iran and the Museum of the Islamic Era. It attracts over 500,000 visitors annually.",
